# Redaction Scanner Selection Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Let teams choose the secret-scanner engines (`redaction.betterleaks.enabled`, `redaction.goredact.enabled`) in committed settings, with fail-closed validation and no silent coverage loss.

**Architecture:** Two per-provider booleans on `RedactionSettings` select which scanner engines run inside `redact.detectAllLayers` (layer 2). goredact is wired as a new region-emitting layer behind an eagerly-constructed shared engine; scanner configuration flows through `strategy.EnsureRedactionConfigured`, which grows an error return for scanner-specific failures, propagated through every checkpoint-writing entry point. A sentinel error (`redact.ErrScannerDegraded`) stops the four silent-fallback write sites from ever writing under a degraded sole scanner.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, github.com/lastpersonlabs/goredact (pinned), existing redact/settings/strategy packages.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-redaction-scanner-selection-design.md` — read it first; it defines every behavior this plan implements.

**Prerequisite:** PR #2042 (betterleaks 1.8.0) must be merged. Branch `feat/redaction-scanner-selection` off `main` after that merge. All work happens on that branch in a dedicated worktree.

**House rules that apply to every task:** `mise run fmt && mise run lint` before every commit; tests extend existing files (never new one-off scenario files); test functions use `t.Parallel()` unless they mutate package-global scanner state; added test lines must not exceed added prod lines across the PR.

